  "description": "EKAVEU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/m c c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H57 Dy4 N16 O9 3+,3(Cl1 O4 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.485-4.929 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.00-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ4-OH)L4]·3ClO4 (C56H57Cl3Dy4N16O21). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
